# Dependencies
node_modules/
# package-lock.json is committed so npm ci can reproduce the reviewed
# dependency tree (see SECURITY.md → Operational Hardening).

# Build output
build/
dist/
coverage/

# Environment variables
# Every .env variant is ignored, not just .env/.env.local: the gateway's
# documented setup (docker-compose.gateway.yml → `cp .env.gateway.example
# .env.gateway`) creates a file holding the live BCONNECT_* service credential,
# and .env.production/.env.staging are the same hazard. The example files are
# re-included because they carry placeholders only. Matches .dockerignore.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.gateway.example

# The credential file scripts/lib/env-path.mjs falls back to.
# `.env.*` does NOT cover it: that pattern matches names BEGINNING with `.env`,
# and this one is `bconnect.env`, which merely ends that way. The fallback is
# in-tree so that someone cloning this has an obvious place to put credentials —
# which makes an ignore rule mandatory rather than tidy.
secrets/

